support:
Of thought and golden image. He can stand
Like Atlas, in the sonnet,—and support
His own heavens pregnant with dynastic stars;

supplies:
Infinite Love where'er we turn our eyes
Appears: this ev'ry creature's wants supplies;
This most is heard in Nature's constant voice,

Upon a guilty land;
Strong in the strength that God supplies,
For truth and justice stand.

supreme:
His to conduct to the immortal plains,
Where heav'n's Supreme in bliss and glory reigns.
There sits, illustrious Sir, thy beauteous spouse;

supremely:
It was a pleasure-place within my soul;
An earthly paradise supremely fair
That lured me from the goal.

The flower deferred, the fruit denied;
But not the peace, supremely won,
Lord Buddha, of thy Lotus-throne.

supports:
who knows the sea depth,
who supports the high pillars
which cut sky from earth;

supernal:
Tho' oft thro' silence infinite I list,
And strain my hearing to supernal sounds;
Tho' oft thro' fateful darkness do I reach,

suppah:
You's hongry as a tramp;
Den hit's eat you suppah right away,
You sta'vin' little scamp.

When I come in f'om de co'n-fiel' aftah wo'kin' ha'd all day,
It 's amazin' nice to fin' my suppah all erpon de way;
An' it 's nice to smell de coffee bubblin' ovah in de pot,

He toss his piccaninny, an' he hum a little chune;
De wokin' all is ovah, an' de suppah comin' soon;
De wo'kin' time 's Decembah, but de restin' time is June,

sup:
Fur good ain't flowin' round this world
Fur every fool to sup;
You 've got to put yore see-ers on,

Beyond the gulf a gleaming strand
Of mansions where the righteous sup;
Who sleep at ease among their trees,

suppress:
By you be shun'd, nor once remit your guard;
Suppress the deadly serpent in its egg.
Ye blooming plants of human race divine,

supercilious:
Around a pile of mountains,
And, supercilious, peer
In shanties by the sides of roads;
